 does not prove that its predecessor path is certain.\n3. Genuinely unresolved branches or missing qualifications. Explain the evidence needed and preserve necessary event-triggered replanning. Do not invent an outcome to fill a queue.\n\nnot_before is an earliest-start condition; the executor also checks actual lot and machine readiness and your submitted machine order. A forecast of now + 1 second is not an exact imminent completion. Do not create one- or two-second plan validity merely to poll it. Under the CURRENT protocol, a retained non-frozen pending task whose not_before is in the past requires your explicit replacement or cancellation; handle those records without resubmitting dispatched work.\n\nOne propose_delta can contain multiple tasks on multiple machines, including ordered follow-on tasks. 'One action' does not mean 'one production task'. 'Small revision' refers to serialized response size. Use the multi-call draft tools only when the complete response really is too large. Choose valid_until to support the intended coverage and any real uncertainty; validity alone is not coverage.\n\nBefore applying a checked candidate, assess whether it addresses the current demand and the near-term resources you inspected. A one-task plan is valid when the facts justify it, but do not use it by default. In the existing reason or selection_note, briefly record the intended coverage, deferred groups and factual reasons, and any unresolved uncertainty. Do not output extra schema fields.\n\nKeep exact lot, operation, visit, machine, batch and order choices model-authored. The host still performs mechanical checks only. This guidance adds no constructor, solver, ranking, automatic selection or silent schedule repair.\n"
